description:
pkix-chain/src/lib.rs:160-169 — The revocation loop uses manual index arithmetic (`i + 1 < chain.len()`, `chain[i + 1]`) to pair each cert with its issuer. Rust idiom is to use `.windows(2)` for adjacent-pair iteration, reducing index noise and making the pairing intent explicit. The last-cert / anchor case can be handled by processing the `chain.last()` element separately before or after the windows loop. This is a readability improvement with no functional impact; the current code is correct. Fix sketch:

```rust
for window in chain.windows(2) {
    revocation.check_revocation(&window[0], &window[1])?;
}
if let Some(last) = chain.last() {
    revocation.check_revocation_against_anchor(last, &anchors[validated.anchor_index])?;
}
```
